/* NOVAMART RETAIL ANALYSIS - DAX SCRIPT
   Adam El Kaissi
   Date: April 2026
   Description: Core measures for calculating financial performance and 
   handling data relationships between Sales and Product tables.
*/

// --- 1. TOTAL REVENUE ---
// Calculates the total value of sales by multiplying quantity by the unit price.
// Since Unit Price lives in the Products table, we use RELATED to pull it into the calculation.
Total Revenue = 
SUMX(
    'sales 1', 
    'sales 1'[Quantity] * RELATED('products 2'[Unit_Price])
)


// --- 2. TOTAL QUANTITY ---
// A simple count of items sold across all transactions.
Total Units Sold = SUM('sales 1'[Quantity])


// --- 3. AVERAGE ORDER VALUE (AOV) ---
// Measures the average dollar amount spent per transaction. 
// Highly useful for identifying if customers are buying premium or budget items.
Average Order Value = 
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue], 
    DISTINCTCOUNT('sales 1'[Transaction_ID]), 
    0
)


// --- 4. CATEGORY REVENUE % ---
// Calculates what percentage of total company revenue a specific category represents.
// Uses ALL() to ignore filters so we can get the grand total for the denominator.
% of Total Revenue = 
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue], 
    CALCULATE([Total Revenue], ALL('products 2'[Category]))
)